# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE LIVE index.html ACTUALLY LOADS FROM vendor/  (updated 2026-08-12)
#
#   vendor/fonts/*.woff2          six self-hosted faces
#   vendor/three.module.min.js    + vendor/three.core.min.js, which it imports
#                                 internally -- shipping only the first gives a
#                                 hard module error
#   vendor/number-flow.min.js     the four hero figures (npm, bundled to one ESM)
#
# vendor/mesh/ is GONE. The page no longer downloads or ships a 3-D model at
# all: the hero object is generated from the cron lines in agents.json. That
# deletes the whole class of problem those files created -- an AGPL asset that
# had already been served publicly once, a v1/v2 pair that had to be kept
# straight by name, and 1.5 MB on disk for a decoration.
#
# vendor/lines/* went with the tract bundle it drew; nothing imports it.
#
# ONE RULE, learned the hard way and still in force: DO NOT use `vendor/*` plus
# a `!vendor/fonts/` re-include. That pattern is correct under git's matcher
# (verified) but Vercel did NOT honour the directory re-include: deployed
# 2026-08-05, /vendor/fonts/IBMPlexSans-400.woff2 came back 404 and the live
# site silently fell back to system fonts. Every exclusion here is therefore
# EXPLICIT, with no negation to get wrong.
#
# After ANY deploy, verify against the deployed URL, not against git: an ignore
# pattern that git accepts proves nothing about how the host treats it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vendored but not used by the live page. GSAP is kept because it became free at
# v3.13 and is the recommended way to do the DOM choreography this page still
# hand-rolls. Excluded until wired.
vendor/gsap.min.js
vendor/ScrollTrigger.min.js
